Local Setup

This is a static project and does not require any build tools or dependencies.

1. Clone the repository:

   ```Bash
   git clone [https://github.com/narcis734/Atelier-LaLyli.git] (https://github.com/narcis734/Atelier-LaLyli.git)
   ```

2. Navigate to the project directory:

   ```Bash
   cd Atelier-LaLyli
   ```

3. Open index.html in your browser or run it with the Live Server extension in Visual Studio Code.

## Registration Form Handling

The registration form utilizes the external service [FormSubmit](https://formsubmit.co/) to deliver booking requests straight to email without requiring a custom backend.

Note: In a production environment, request handling would ideally be moved to a dedicated backend API with anti-spam protection and database storage.

## Roadmap & Planned Improvements

[ ] Migrate the UI to a modern framework (React).

[ ] Develop a backend service with database integration.

[ ] Interactive calendar displaying real-time available slots.

[ ] Admin panel authentication for managing workshops.

[ ] Workshop filtering and sorting options.

[ ] Image optimization and Lighthouse performance audit.

[ ] Unit and integration testing for interactive UI components.

[ ] Dedicated details page for each workshop.

[ ] Multi-language support (Romanian / English).

## Project Goal

This project demonstrates the ability to build a complete, responsive, and interactive frontend interface using core web technologies, with attention to design, accessibility, and user experience.

